An earlier version of this integration saved an entity type for these BACnet objects that ignores whether the object is commandable:

{objects}

Non-commandable objects set to a writable type (switch, number) usually reject writes; commandable objects stuck on a read-only type (sensor) can't be controlled. Remove these overrides to return the objects to their default type, or keep them if you chose these types deliberately (some devices accept writes without a Priority Array). The integration reloads either way and doesn't ask again for kept objects.
